-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Bubbler
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Bubbler (1987)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         85d7841306333321838d372ea8797ff2

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    MatGubbins' colours: the bubble white, the creatures green, the
              targets red and cyan, the floors grey with the original's yellow
              walls and slopes; the panel, score and gauges unchanged. No
              outlines added. Source: Enhanced colours: MatGubbins, from his
              Spec256 conversion of the game.

  Pace        original (-0.17% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; nine
              original scenes, three raster phases each, 120 updates, at the
              player's own update; every whole and steady trial faster than
              the original, by 0.1 to 1.6%)

  Changes     1.0: Enhanced colours from MatGubbins' Spec256 conversion, drawn
              in the original order with its masks on a double-buffered Layer
              2 view; the original loading screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the
              whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed restored
              after every hook; four cheats from the archive.

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu A for one player or B for two, choose
              keyboard, Kempston, cursor or Interface II for each player, then
              0 to start. The default is the original game, picture and all:
              its play area is drawn in one colour, so it never had colour
              clash; the patch gives it Sinclair's whole 48K ROM so it runs on
              NextZXOS 26.11. Enhanced paints the bubble, creatures, items and
              floors in their own colours, drawn on the Next's Layer 2 so the
              original's masks, scenery and panel stay as they were; off by
              default. The original 48K game with its beeper sound; fits a 1MB
              Next. Known issues: the original's stepped movement, deliberate
              pauses and low update rate remain; in JNext it runs 0.1 to 1.6
              percent faster than the original in every scene measured.
              Missing: not reached in testing: natural play to the end (all
              five stages reached with the next-level cheat), joysticks;
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite time
   2  Infinite lives
   3  Immunity
   4  Next level on life loss

  The archive's four POKEs match this release once the original loader's
  inversion is allowed for; the patch stores them inverted so the game gets
  the right bytes. Infinite time stops time running out but the clock still
  counts; Immunity keeps the start-of-life protection and must be on before
  play starts.

